              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Kannada for to peep, then the Kannada for a fare."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಹಮಾಲಿ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಹಮಾಲಿ — hamāli — \"a porter\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಹಮಾಲಿ ನನ್ನ ಎರಡು ಸೂಟ್ಕೇಸ್ಗಳನ್ನು ಹೊತ್ತನು. hamāli nanna eraḍu sūṭkēsgaḷannu hottanu. The porter carried my two suitcases."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: ಹಮಾಲಿಗಳು, hamāligaḷu."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "At stations porters wear a red shirt and a numbered badge; ಕೂಲಿ also names them."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಹಮಾಲಿ (hamāli) is usually traced to Arabic ḥammāl, \"a carrier, a porter\", which reached Kannada through Hindustani or Marathi."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
