        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಹೇರು",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಹೇರು — hēru — \"to load; to impose\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಅವರು ವಾಹನದ ಮೇಲೆ ಸಾಮಾನು ಹೇರಿದರು. avaru vāhanada mēle sāmānu hēridaru. They loaded the luggage on top of the vehicle."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): ಹೇರಿದೆ, hēride."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What is loaded takes -ಅನ್ನು or no ending; figuratively, ತೆರಿಗೆ ಹೇರು (hēru), to impose a tax."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಹೇರು (hēru) is native Dravidian: DEDR 4446 lists Kannada pēṟu, \"to lift up and put on, to load; a load\", the older form with the p- that modern Kannada turns into h-. The same article holds Telugu pērcu, to pile up."
            }
          ]
        },
